<task id="012" project="spaarkeai-compose-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-03 1b upload -&gt; transient mount (flip send_workspace_artifact + feed bytes)</title>
    <phase>1 Entry</phase>
    <status>completed</status>
    <estimated-hours>16</estimated-hours>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <dependencies>none</dependencies>
    <blocks>017</blocks>
    <tags>bff-api,api,frontend</tags>
    <rigor-hint reason="Modifies .cs (handler + endpoint) and .tsx; flips an LLM tool refusal contract; BFF-touching; FULL per TASK-INDEX">FULL</rigor-hint>
    <model-tier reason="Cross-surface change (LLM tool description + endpoint activation + client mount) that alters an established refusal contract — higher blast radius; opus per TASK-INDEX">opus</model-tier>
    <parallel-group>W2</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe reason="Shares ComposeWorkspace/ComposeEmptyState with 010/011 on the client leg — serialize 010 -&gt; 011 -&gt; 012; BFF leg (handler/endpoint) is independent">false</parallel-safe>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Today an Assistant-uploaded file cannot open in Compose: `SendWorkspaceArtifactHandler` explicitly
    REFUSES session-uploaded file ids as a Compose pre-seed (its tool description says the tab "opens
    empty for session files"), and `POST /api/compose/upload` returns 501. The upload flow already
    RETAINS the original `File` bytes. FR-03: flip that refusal for the Compose-mount path and feed the
    retained upload bytes into the editor's source-agnostic `docxBytes` seam as a TRANSIENT working
    draft — so "open in Compose" on an uploaded `.docx` shows its content instead of an empty tab.
    Activate `POST /api/compose/upload` as needed to serve the retained bytes. No `sprk_document` is
    created until first Save (create-on-save, FR-05 / task 013).
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Full-stack developer: .NET Minimal API + the Spaarke AI chat-tool handlers on the server, and the
    Compose widget + attachments hooks on the client. You alter an established LLM-tool refusal contract
    carefully and keep the change scoped to the Compose-mount path.
  </role>

  <goal>
    Uploading a `.docx` in the Assistant and choosing "open in Compose" mounts the file's retained bytes
    into the TipTap editor transiently (content visible, no empty tab); `POST /api/compose/upload` is
    activated to serve those bytes where the client needs a fetch; `send_workspace_artifact` no longer
    refuses session-upload ids for the Compose-mount path; no `sprk_document` is created until Save.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      As-built (design.md §5): upload bytes go to `/api/ai/chat/sessions/{id}/documents` for RAG; the
      `send_workspace_artifact` tool refuses session-file ids as a Compose pre-seed and tells the user
      the tab opens empty; `POST /api/compose/upload` = 501. The mount seam is source-agnostic, so the
      short reach is: (1) stop refusing on the Compose-mount path, (2) route the retained upload `File`
      bytes into `docxBytes`. This differs from 010 (local picker) — here the bytes originate from a
      session upload the Assistant already holds.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file purpose="flip-refusal" edit="true">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Handlers/SendWorkspaceArtifactHandler.cs</file>
      <file purpose="activate-endpoint" edit="true">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ComposeEndpoints.cs</file>
      <file purpose="client-mount" edit="true">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeWorkspace.tsx</file>
      <file purpose="upload-bytes" edit="maybe">src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/components/conversation/useAttachments.ts</file>
      <file purpose="mount-seam" edit="false">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeEditor.tsx</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <notes>
      SendWorkspaceArtifactHandler.cs: the refusal text lives in the tool description + validation
      (~lines 167/191/314); `ComposeLaunchContext` (~line 657) is how a Compose section opens LOADED
      rather than empty. ComposeEndpoints.cs: the `Upload` handler returns 501 at ~line 108 with a
      message steering callers to the Assistant pipeline; activate it to return/serve retained bytes for
      the Compose-mount path. Keep RAG-upload behavior intact for non-Compose flows.
    </notes>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-013">`Services/Compose` (and any Compose-mount code) never injects `IOpenAiClient`/executor/routing types; the upload-mount path is deterministic file handling, not AI dispatch.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-039">No new AI dispatch endpoint; activating `POST /api/compose/upload` is a file-serving route, not a dispatch route; no string-key routing.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-008">`POST /api/compose/upload`, once activated, applies `RequireAuthorization()` (endpoint filter authz) — it is NOT health/ping.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Client fetch of upload bytes uses `@spaarke/auth`; never a raw Bearer.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-007">Any SPE/Graph access stays behind the `SpeFileStore`/Infrastructure facade — no `Microsoft.Graph` types leak up.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Flip the refusal ONLY for the Compose-mount path; RAG upload behavior for other flows is unchanged.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">MUST NOT create a `sprk_document` on upload-mount — creation is Save-time (013).</constraint>
    <constraint source="bff-hygiene">This task adds/activates a BFF endpoint — state the Placement Justification, measure publish-size delta vs the 49.63 MB baseline, and run the CVE scan per §10.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>ai/chat-tool-handlers, compose/entry-paths, minimal-api-auth, spe</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-013-ai-architecture.md</file>
