  <justification component="Activated POST /api/compose/upload + flipped send_workspace_artifact refusal">
    <existing>The upload endpoint stub (501) and the refusal-carrying `send_workspace_artifact` tool both already exist; upload bytes are already retained.</existing>
    <extension>Activate the existing stub and narrow the existing refusal; extend the client to route retained bytes into the existing `docxBytes` seam — no new component/service.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without this, "open in Compose" on an uploaded file opens an empty tab (the concrete R1 UAT complaint); FR-03 unmet and the 1b entry-path success criterion fails.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Load spec.md FR-03 + `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`; state the Placement Justification. Read SendWorkspaceArtifactHandler.cs, ComposeEndpoints.cs Upload handler, useAttachments.ts, ComposeWorkspace.tsx.</step>
    <step order="1">Narrow the `send_workspace_artifact` refusal: allow session-upload ids on the Compose-mount path; update the tool description so it no longer tells the user the tab opens empty for session files (keep other refusals intact).</step>
    <step order="2">Activate `POST /api/compose/upload` to serve/accept the retained upload bytes for the Compose-mount path, with `RequireAuthorization()` and SPE access behind the facade; keep the RAG-upload route unchanged.</step>
    <step order="3">On the client, route the retained upload `File` bytes (or the upload-endpoint response) into `state.docxBytes` transiently, marking the editor dirty and pointer-less so first Save runs create-on-save.</step>
    <step order="4">Add/update BFF unit tests (SendWorkspaceArtifactHandler + upload endpoint) per NFR-08 and ui-tests for the client mount. Build BFF + package; measure publish-size delta; run CVE scan.</step>
    <step order="5">Run code-review + adr-check (Step 9.5). Update TASK-INDEX + current-task.md.</step>
  </steps>

