  <ui-tests>
    <ui-test name="upload-mounts-content">Simulating "open in Compose" on an uploaded `.docx` mounts its retained bytes into the editor (content visible, empty state gone) — not an empty tab.</ui-test>
    <ui-test name="no-create-on-mount">Upload-mount issues no `sprk_document` create; the editor is dirty so Save triggers create-on-save.</ui-test>
    <ui-test name="dark-mode">Editor renders correctly in dark mode (ADR-021) for the upload-mounted document.</ui-test>
  </ui-tests>

  <acceptance-criteria testable="true">
    <criterion testable="true">Uploading a `.docx` in the Assistant then choosing "open in Compose" renders its content in the editor (no empty tab).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`send_workspace_artifact` no longer refuses session-upload ids for the Compose-mount path, and its description no longer claims the tab opens empty for session files.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`POST /api/compose/upload` no longer returns 501 for the Compose-mount path and applies `RequireAuthorization()` (ADR-008).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No `sprk_document` is created on upload-mount; the editor is dirty so first Save runs create-on-save (FR-05).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">RAG-upload behavior for non-Compose flows is unchanged (regression check).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No `Microsoft.Graph` type leaks above the SpeFileStore/Infrastructure facade (ADR-007); NetArchTest facade rule stays green.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">(negative) An unauthenticated call to `POST /api/compose/upload` is rejected (401/403).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF publish-size delta is reported vs the 49.63 MB baseline; no new HIGH CVE; BFF + package build succeed; unit + ui tests pass.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

