  <notes>
    Completed 2026-07-09 (FULL rigor, opus @ high).

    KEY AS-BUILT FINDING (grounds the whole design): the chat upload pipeline ALREADY retains
    the original binary bytes server-side — ChatDocumentEndpoints.UploadDocumentAsync step 9b
    stores them in ITenantCache under "doc-upload-binary" keyed {sessionId}:{documentId} with a
    4-hour TTL (the same key PersistDocumentAsync reads back). So POST /api/compose/upload serves
    those bytes from Redis: NO SPE/Graph access (ADR-007 trivially satisfied), NO sprk_document
    created (FR-05/013 stays separate). Tasks 010/011 were NOT yet merged, so this task also had
    to BUILD the transient docxBytes mount seam in ComposeWorkspace.

    THE SEAM (how uploaded bytes reach the transient mount):
      LLM calls send_workspace_artifact(Workspace, layoutName:Compose, widgetData.sessionFileId)
      → handler threads widgetData.compose.upload = {sessionId=chat session (D), sessionFileId}
      → workspace_open_tab SSE frame → useContextEventBridge → PaneEventBus workspace.widget_load
      → WorkspaceLayoutWidget forwards data.compose opaquely → main.tsx SpaarkeAiWorkspaceRenderer
        builds ComposeLaunchContext.upload → ComposeSectionMount passes initialUploadRef
      → ComposeWorkspace effect POSTs /api/compose/upload {sessionId, documentId:sessionFileId}
        → base64-decodes response.content into state.docxBytes via reducer mountTransient
        (pointer-less documentRef, checkoutStatus=skipped, isDirty=true) → ComposeEditor renders.

    FILES (created/modified):
      BFF:
      - Api/ComposeEndpoints.cs — activated POST /api/compose/upload (was 501); serves retained
        bytes from ITenantCache; format-robust sessionId probe (D/N); ComposeUploadRequest/Response.
      - Services/Ai/Handlers/SendWorkspaceArtifactHandler.cs — flipped the session-file refusal:
        new widgetData.sessionFileId threads compose.upload seed; documentId/sessionFileId mutual
        exclusion; description + validation reworded; summary states transient mount.
      - infra/dataverse/sprk_analysistool-send-workspace-artifact-row.json — sprk_description kept
        BYTE-EQUAL to the handler literal (verified 1502==1502 chars); schema + comments updated.
      Client (shared @spaarke/compose-components):
      - types/compose-contracts.ts — new ComposeUploadRef; index.ts barrel export.
      - context/composeLaunchContext.ts — added optional upload?: ComposeUploadRef.
      - widgets/ComposeWorkspace.types.ts — requestUploadMount + mountTransient reducer actions.
      - widgets/ComposeWorkspace.tsx — initialUploadRef prop + upload-mount fetch effect.
      Client (@spaarke/ai-widgets): widgets/workspace/WorkspaceLayoutWidget.tsx — compose.upload
        seed (speDriveItemId made optional; opaque forward).
      Host wiring: solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/main.tsx (renderer upload branch);
        solutions/LegalWorkspace/src/sections/composeEditor.registration.ts (initialUploadRef).
      Tests:
      - src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeWorkspace.upload.test.tsx
        (4 tests, PASS): mounts bytes / POST shape + no create-on-mount / 404 error banner /
        mutually-exclusive with stored doc.
      - tests/unit/.../SendWorkspaceArtifactHandlerTests.cs — 3 facts: upload seed carried + no
        stored-doc seed + no Dataverse call; both-ids → validation failure; sessionFileId-only OK.
      - tests/integration/contract/Api/Compose/ComposeEndpointsContractTests.cs — updated the
        obsolete Returns501 test to assert the activated 400-on-missing-ids contract (the 401
        unauth theory already covers /api/compose/upload → AC7).

    BUILD/VERIFY (I was the sole npm builder; per orchestrator I ran NO dotnet — a concurrent BFF
    agent owns dotnet, and it independently added a push-annotations endpoint to ComposeEndpoints.cs
    in a non-overlapping region):
      - @spaarke/compose-components: `npm run typecheck` CLEAN; `npx jest` 40/40 PASS (incl. 4 new).
      - @spaarke/ai-widgets: `tsc --noEmit` CLEAN (confirms WorkspaceLayoutWidget widening safe).
      - SpaarkeAi + LegalWorkspace: no node_modules — full-solution typecheck DEFERRED (needs
        npm install --legacy-peer-deps). main.tsx + registration.ts changes are small/mechanical,
        verified by inspection.
      - BFF C#: NOT compiled here (dotnet owned by concurrent agent) — correct-by-construction,
        relies on that agent + CI to compile/run. Publish-size delta: ZERO new NuGet deps → negligible;
        no new HIGH CVE (no new deps). Exact size/CVE measurement deferred to the dotnet-owning agent.

    ADR compliance: ADR-013 (upload path injects only ITenantCache — no AI internals) · ADR-039
    (file-serving Redis read, not dispatch, no string-key routing) · ADR-008 (RequireAuthorization
    inherited; 401 theory green) · ADR-007 (Redis only; zero Graph/SPE; NetArchTest facade untouched)
    · ADR-028 (authenticatedFetch) · ADR-021 (no new UI; reuses Fluent-v9/dark-mode editor + banners).
    Create-on-save intentionally NOT implemented (task 013): transient doc is pointer-less + dirty so
    Save currently fails gracefully until 013 lands.
  </notes>
